### Describe the bug

According to the [CaseBlockEvaluation spec](https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/ecmascript-language-statements-and-declarations.html#sec-runtime-semantics-caseblockevaluation), case expressions in case clauses placed after `default` case should not be evaluated when there is any match case before `default` case.

### Input code

```typescript
const k = (() => {
    const x = 'asdf';
    switch (x) {
        case x:
        default:
        case console.log("hi"):
    }
})();
```


